  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law posits that the negation of a conjunction of two statements is equivalent to the disjunction of the negated individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows.\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)=¬A∨¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(5>3\\text{ and }7\\text{ is even}) & ≡¬((5>3)∧(7\\text{ is even})) \\\\  & ≡¬(5>3)∨¬(7\\text{ is even}) \\\\  & ≡(5\\le 3)∨(7\\text{ is odd}) \\\\  & ≡5\\le 3\\text{ or }7\\text{ is odd}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
